{"title":"Plane","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\">mathematics</a>, a <b>plane</b> is a two-<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Dimension\" title=\"Dimension\">dimensional</a> object that is infinitely <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Length\" title=\"Length\"> long</a> and wide, but has no <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Thick&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Thick (page does not exist)\">thickness</a> and zero curvature.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Euclidean_Geometry\">Euclidean Geometry</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Euclidean Geometry\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In Euclidean <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>, a plane is defined by:\n</p>\n<ul><li>three <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Linear\" title=\"Linear\"> non-collinear</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Point\" title=\"Point\">points</a></li>\n<li>a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> and a point not on the line</li>\n<li>two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Intersect\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Intersect\">intersecting</a> lines</li>\n<li>two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Parallel\" title=\"Parallel\">parallel</a> lines</li></ul>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>A line can intersect a plane in a single point, or it can be in the plane.\n</p><p>Two planes <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular\" title=\"Perpendicular\">perpendicular</a> to the same line are parallel to each other.\n</p><p>Two lines perpendicular to the same plane are parallel to each other.\n</p><p>Two planes can be parallel, or they can intersect in a line.\n</p><p>If two lines are perpendicular to each other and one of them is in a plane, then the other is either also in that plane or perpendicular to the plane.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Plane&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hyperplane&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Hyperplane (page does not exist)\">Hyperplane</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Plane&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017135925\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.017 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 26/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 256/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.993      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.993      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:4053:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017135925 and revision id 198992. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}